{"id": "unknown-2026-07-20-011", "date": "2026-07-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Netherlands proposes stricter rules for solar near airports", "content": "<p>The Netherlands is working on a temporary framework governing permits for solar near airports. Trade association Holland Solar has said there is a lack of convincing evidence as to why solar panels have to meet stricter reflection requirements than other surfaces.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/20/netherlands-proposes-stricter-rules-for-solar-near-airports/\">Netherlands proposes stricter rules for solar near airports </a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/20/netherlands-proposes-stricter-rules-for-solar-near-airports/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-20-012", "date": "2026-07-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Nibe unveils residential propane air-to-water heat pumps reaching 5.53 COP", "content": "<p>Nibe has launched the S2060 series, a range of inverter-controlled air-to-water heat pumps using propane refrigerant for residential and small commercial applications. The monoblock units deliver up to 10 kW of heating capacity and operate with flow temperatures of up to 75 C. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/20/nibe-unveils-residential-propane-air-to-water-heat-pumps-reaching-5-53-cop/\">Nibe unveils residential propane air-to-water heat pumps reaching 5.53 COP</a", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/20/nibe-unveils-residential-propane-air-to-water-heat-pumps-reaching-5-53-cop/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-20-013", "date": "2026-07-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Fraunhofer CSP develops ultrathin glass-glass PV modules strengthened by special coating", "content": "<p>A new glass coating technology developed by Exxosqel and Fraunhofer CSP could enable thinner, lighter PV modules by improving glass strength and reducing material use.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/20/fraunhofer-csp-develops-ultrathin-glass-glass-pv-modules-strengthened-by-special-coating/\">Fraunhofer CSP develops ultrathin glass-glass PV modules strengthened by special coating</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/20/fraunhofer-csp-develops-ultrathin-glass-glass-pv-modules-strengthened-by-special-coating/", "type": "rss"}]}
